{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And He buried him in the valley</b> — defective alef. So that no man knew his burial place. Even Moses' teacher did not know, for Moses too is called 'man.' Rather, the Unique One of the world, blessed be He and blessed be His name, and blessed be His remembrance, amen:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The lemma cites 'בגי' defective (without alef), referring to בגיא of Deut. 34:6. The phrase 'מרע\"ה' likely abbreviates 'מורנו רבינו ע\"ה' (our teacher our master, peace be upon him) or similar; rendered as 'Moses' teacher.' The expanded doxology 'ב\"ה וב\"ש וברוך זכרו' is rendered by its standard expansion: 'ברוך הוא וברוך שמו וברוך זכרו'."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:32.459055133Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}